msgid ""
"Google Cloud Functions (Serverless) with Quarkus REST, Undertow, or Reactive "
"Routes"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `quarkus-google-cloud-functions-http` extension allows you to write "
"microservices with Quarkus REST (Jakarta REST),\n"
"Undertow (Servlet), Reactive Routes, or xref:funqy-http.adoc[Funqy HTTP], "
"and make these microservices deployable to the Google Cloud Functions "
"runtime."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"One Google Cloud Functions deployment can represent any number of Jakarta "
"REST, Servlet, Reactive Routes, or xref:funqy-http.adoc[Funqy HTTP] "
"endpoints."
msgstr ""

msgid "This technology is considered {extension-status}."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In _preview_, backward compatibility and presence in the ecosystem is not "
"guaranteed.\n"
"Specific improvements might require changing configuration or APIs, and "
"plans to become _stable_ are under way.\n"
"Feedback is welcome on our https://groups.google.com/d/forum/quarkus-"
"dev[mailing list] or as issues in our https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"issues[GitHub issue tracker]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For a full list of possible statuses, check our https://quarkus.io/faq/#what-"
"are-the-extension-statuses[FAQ entry]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

msgid "To complete this guide, you need:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Roughly 15 minutes"
msgstr ""

msgid "An IDE"
msgstr ""

msgid "JDK 17+ installed with `JAVA_HOME` configured appropriately"
msgstr ""

msgid "Apache Maven {maven-version}"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Optionally the xref:cli-tooling.adoc[Quarkus CLI] if you want to use it"
msgstr ""

msgid "https://cloud.google.com/[A Google Cloud Account]. Free accounts work."
msgstr ""

msgid "https://cloud.google.com/sdk[Cloud SDK CLI Installed]"
msgstr ""

msgid "Solution"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This guide walks you through generating a sample project followed by "
"creating three HTTP endpoints\n"
"written with Jakarta REST APIs, Servlet APIs, Reactive Routes, or xref:funqy-"
"http.adoc[Funqy HTTP] APIs. Once built, you will be able to deploy\n"
"the project to Google Cloud."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you don't want to follow all these steps, you can go right to the "
"completed example."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Clone the Git repository: `git clone {quickstarts-clone-url}`, or download "
"an {quickstarts-archive-url}[archive]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The solution is located in the `google-cloud-functions-http-quickstart` link:"
"{quickstarts-tree-url}/google-cloud-functions-http-quickstart[directory]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Creating the Maven Deployment Project"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Create an application with the `quarkus-google-cloud-functions-http` "
"extension.\n"
"You can use the following Maven command to create it:"
msgstr ""

msgid "CLI"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To create a Gradle project, add the `--gradle` or `--gradle-kotlin-dsl` "
"option."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For more information about how to install and use the Quarkus CLI, see the "
"xref:cli-tooling.adoc[Quarkus CLI] guide."
msgstr ""

msgid "Maven"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To create a Gradle project, add the `-DbuildTool=gradle` or `-DbuildTool="
"gradle-kotlin-dsl` option."
msgstr ""

msgid "For Windows users:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If using cmd, (don't use backward slash `\\` and put everything on the same "
"line)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If using Powershell, wrap `-D` parameters in double quotes e.g. `\"-"
"DprojectArtifactId={create-app-artifact-id}\"`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Login to Google Cloud"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Login to Google Cloud is necessary for deploying the application. It can be "
"done as follows:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Creating the endpoints"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For this example project, we will create four endpoints, one for Quarkus "
"REST (Jakarta REST), one for Undertow (Servlet),\n"
"one for Reactive routes and one for xref:funqy-http.adoc[Funqy HTTP]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"These various endpoints are for demonstration purposes.\n"
"For real life applications, you should choose one of these technologies and "
"stick to it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you don't need endpoints of each type, you can remove the corresponding "
"extensions from your `pom.xml`."
msgstr ""

