msgid "Build and Deploy to Google Cloud"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Package your application using the standard `mvn clean package` command.\n"
"The result of the previous command is a single JAR file inside the `target/"
"deployment` directory that contains the classes and the dependencies of the "
"project."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Then you will be able to use `gcloud` to deploy your function to Google "
"Cloud."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The entry point must always be set to `io.quarkus.gcp.functions.http."
"QuarkusHttpFunction` as this is the class that integrates Cloud Functions "
"with Quarkus."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The first time you launch this command, you can have the following error "
"message:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This means that Cloud Build is not activated yet. To overcome this error, "
"open the URL shown in the error, follow the instructions and then wait a few "
"minutes before retrying the command."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This command will give you as output a `url` that points to your function."
msgstr ""

msgid "You can then call your endpoints via:"
msgstr ""

msgid "For Jakarta REST: `{url}/hello`"
msgstr ""

msgid "For servlet: `{url}/servlet/hello`"
msgstr ""

msgid "For Reactive Routes: `{url}/vertx/hello`"
msgstr ""

msgid "For Funqy: `{url}/funqy`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Testing locally"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The easiest way to locally test your function is using the Cloud Function "
"invoker JAR."
msgstr ""

msgid "You can download it via Maven using the following command:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Before using the invoker, you first need to build your function via `mvn "
"package`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Then you can use it to launch your function locally."
msgstr ""

msgid "Your endpoints will be available on http://localhost:8080."
msgstr ""

msgid "What&#8217;s next?"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can use our xref:funqy-gcp-functions.adoc[Google Cloud Functions Funqy "
"binding] to use Funqy,\n"
"a provider-agnostic function as a service framework, that allow to deploy "
"HTTP function or Background function to Google Cloud."
msgstr ""
